/public
/.tola/
.DS_Store
# Live `mt` captures, regenerated by `just docs::gen` (www/generate.sh).
/generated
# Favicon/apple-touch-icon rasters, regenerated from assets/images/logo.svg by
# www/generate.sh on every build — logo.svg stays the only hand-maintained copy.
/assets/images/favicon-32.png
/assets/images/apple-touch-icon.png
# rsvg-convert writes those two rasters through GIO, which saves atomically: a
# `.goutputstream-XXXXXX` sibling, then a rename over the target. The sibling
# lives for milliseconds, and unignored it was an INPUT — mmz resolved it while
# hashing `secrets-tree` for a parallel `just check-secrets`, then exited 8
# ("input www/assets/images/.goutputstream-RLQRU3 disappeared after it was
# resolved") with no secret involved, once in three runs
# (truth/tasks/check-secrets-races-the-docs-arm-over-www-generated.typ). Ignored
# here rather than redirected in www/generate.sh: this file is the one
# declaration of what the docs build owns that both readers of the tree consult
# — mmz filters its input walk by it, and .gitleaks.toml restates it by hand
# under the arm-four check — so the answer belongs where they already look, and
# it holds for any future writer that saves the same way.
.goutputstream-*
